{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The USB hub fits my growing collection of peripherals and my recent effort to organize my desk; individual switches would make those devices easier to manage.",
    "The flash drive would help me move files and keep installation media handy, while the Bluetooth adapter could support a wireless controller for retro gaming if compatibility checks out. Both have practical uses alongside my computer projects."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Another HDMI cable or pair of wired earphones repeats needs I have already covered; similarity to something I bought does not mean I need another one now.",
    "The optical cable, USB-C accessories, and large internal SSD require particular connections or upgrade needs I have not identified. The smart speaker also lacks a clear role in my current computer setup."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying cables and headphones seems to have been taken as a continuing desire for more cables and headphones, without a specific new use.",
    "My interest in computer accessories seems to have been stretched to include electronics that depend on devices or connections I have not shown I use."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My cable management kit, cable ties, and headphone mount suggest that making an existing setup more organized and convenient matters to me.",
    "My Raspberry Pi, retro-style case, and wireless keyboard make practical project accessories plausible next choices, but compatibility and a concrete task still determine whether I would choose them."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my interest in practical computer projects, but missed the difference between useful additions, duplicate purchases, and accessories without a confirmed need."
}"}
